This is **static image object detection** where:
- Users select a **single image** from gallery/camera
- The app sends **one prediction request** per image
- Gets **one prediction response** back
- No continuous video stream processing

The app performs **batch/on-demand object detection** on static images, not real-time video analysis.

And yes, the backend is **TensorFlow Serving** containerized and deployed on **Google Cloud Run** at the endpoint `mobilenet-ssd-api-879557471105.europe-southwest1.run.app`, which hosts the MobileNet SSD model for inference.

Thanks for the correction - the app is designed for single image analysis, not continuous real-time detection.
